WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.768
Be honest.

2
00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:04.832
How do your pupils use AI?

3
00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:07.385
For most, it's a search box:

4
00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:09.602
type the question, copy the answer.

5
00:00:10.027 --> 00:00:12.982
When Anthropic looked at university students' chats,

6
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:16.260
almost half asked straight for an answer, or finished work.

7
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.147
Does that matter?

8
00:00:19.504 --> 00:00:23.849
Researchers tested it with nearly a thousand high-school maths pupils in Türkiye.

9
00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:28.791
While they practised with an open chatbot, their scores jumped by 48 percent.

10
00:00:29.216 --> 00:00:31.647
Then the AI was taken away for the exam.

11
00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:35.583
They scored 17 percent lower than pupils who never had AI.

12
00:00:36.143 --> 00:00:37.199
Practice soared.

13
00:00:37.354 --> 00:00:38.448
Learning sank.

14
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:43.569
But a tutor version, which gave hints instead of answers, did no harm.

15
00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:46.654
Why does it go wrong?

16
00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:47.877
Four traps.

17
00:00:48.235 --> 00:00:49.511
It makes things up:

18
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:55.813
a South African court could trace only two of the nine cases a legal team had cited, probably invented by AI.

19
00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:57.595
It agrees with you:

20
00:00:57.548 --> 00:01:04.161
Say “I think the answer is 12, right?” and many chatbots will agree, even when 12 is wrong.

21
00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:08.894
It can be unfair, because it learnt from human writing, bias included.

22
00:01:09.184 --> 00:01:10.867
And it can be out of date.

23
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.611
So keep your brain doing the work.

24
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:17.542
Five power-ups, all backed by research:

25
00:01:17.629 --> 00:01:18.792
test yourself,

26
00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:19.970
space it out,

27
00:01:19.882 --> 00:01:20.903
mix it up,

28
00:01:20.815 --> 00:01:21.942
explain it,

29
00:01:21.854 --> 00:01:23.048
make it yourself.

30
00:01:23.405 --> 00:01:27.138
AI can power every one, if you ask it to quiz you, not tell you.

31
00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.060
Both booklets teach one routine.

32
00:01:31.283 --> 00:01:32.560
Attempt it first.

33
00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.907
Name where you're stuck.

34
00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.278
Ask for one hint.

35
00:01:35.298 --> 00:01:36.462
Check the reply.

36
00:01:36.482 --> 00:01:39.750
Then close the AI, and solve a fresh question alone.

37
00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:44.312
Need help? Climb the hint ladder only as high as you need.

38
00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.685
The full answer is the last resort.

39
00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:49.629
Prompt like a pro.

40
00:01:49.784 --> 00:01:52.916
Google found the best prompts average about 21 words;

41
00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.921
most people type fewer than nine.

42
00:01:55.211 --> 00:01:56.493
Say who you are,

43
00:01:56.378 --> 00:01:57.306
the topic,

44
00:01:57.191 --> 00:01:58.234
what you tried,

45
00:01:58.119 --> 00:01:59.346
the help you want,

46
00:01:59.231 --> 00:02:01.805
and the rules: “Don’t give me the answer.”

47
00:02:03.555 --> 00:02:04.618
Then check it.

48
00:02:04.706 --> 00:02:06.034
Does it match your book?

49
00:02:05.986 --> 00:02:07.305
Does it make sense?

50
00:02:07.325 --> 00:02:09.469
Never use AI to check itself.

51
00:02:09.894 --> 00:02:11.885
Keep your private details private.

52
00:02:11.972 --> 00:02:13.332
AI is not a friend.

53
00:02:13.487 --> 00:02:15.236
And never fake a real person:

54
00:02:15.256 --> 00:02:17.170
deepfake abuse is abuse.

55
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.663
The world has already moved.

56
00:02:20.818 --> 00:02:23.763
UCT has stopped using AI-detection scores.

57
00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:26.464
Students must explain their work out loud,

58
00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:28.151
and declare their AI use.

59
00:02:28.508 --> 00:02:29.785
What should they build?

60
00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:31.029
Deep knowledge,

61
00:02:30.914 --> 00:02:32.198
thinking out loud,

62
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:33.504
and AI fluency.

63
00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:36.058
Expertise is what makes AI useful.

64
00:02:37.808 --> 00:02:42.856
So I wrote two booklets, built on this research, with AI as my co-pilot.

65
00:02:43.146 --> 00:02:46.434
For Grades 7 to 9: Brain On, AI On.

66
00:02:46.521 --> 00:02:49.969
AI is a power tool. Your brain is the power.

67
00:02:50.326 --> 00:02:54.350
For Grades 10 to 12: Co-Pilot, Not Autopilot.

68
00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:57.777
You fly the plane. AI helps you navigate.

69
00:02:58.134 --> 00:02:59.467
They're ready to try.

70
00:03:00.027 --> 00:03:03.757
Because the measure that counts is what you can do when the AI is switched off.
